Package: driftmapR
Title: Align Repeated Coordinate Maps and Measure Relative Movement
Version: 0.0.3.9000
Authors@R: person("Prototype", "Maintainer", email = "maintainer@example.org",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A development prototype for ingesting repeated two-dimensional
    coordinate maps, aligning them using orthogonal Procrustes transformations,
    and measuring reference-relative entity movement. Supports changing entity
    sets, optional alignment anchors, translation, reflection, rotation, and
    optional isotropic scaling. Provides explicit transformation diagnostics
    and descriptive trajectory plots. Matches supplied cluster identities by
    maximum shared-entity overlap, with explicit assignment and ambiguity
    diagnostics. Includes centered PCA and classical multidimensional scaling
    adapters with retained inputs, preprocessing, and spectral diagnostics.
    No inferential uncertainty is estimated.
